<title>THAILAND: Canada signs 1.0 mln tonne wheat deal with Thais.</title>
<headline>Canada signs 1.0 mln tonne wheat deal with Thais.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board has signed a letter of agreement with seven Thai flour mills to sell more than 1.0 million tonnes of wheat to them over the next five years, a Canadian government statement said on Friday.</p>
<p>The statement said the business was worth C$250 million at current wheat prices.  </p>
<p>The Thai flour mills involved in the deal are United Flour Mill Co Ltd, Siam Flour Trading Co Ltd, Laemthong Corp Ltd, Thai Flour Mill Industry Co Ltd, Bangkok Flour Mill Co Ltd, Nisshin-STC Flour Milling Co Ltd, and Kerry-Glory Flour Mill Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The Canadian Wheat Board exports wheat and barley to 70 countries around the world.</p>
</text>
